course: dictionary
lesson: 8173
title: Resist: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Resist is a verb: resist, resists, resisted, resisting. It can have more than one meaning, so the context tells you which one you need. The main meaning is to fight against something or refuse to accept it. «Enslaved people resisted in many ways, from revolts on ships to running away» means they fought back against being treated unfairly.
explain: To resist something tempting means to stop yourself from doing or having it. In everyday life, you might try to resist eating all the chocolate. The clue is the tempting thing: you want it, but you hold yourself back.
explain: In science, resist means not to be harmed by something, or to slow down or oppose a flow. «Reinforced concrete has steel bars inside it so it can resist stretching as well as squashing.» Swap in your meaning: the concrete does not stretch easily, so it stays strong. Check that your meaning still makes sense in the sentence.
fact: Resist means to fight against something, refuse to accept it, or stop yourself from doing something tempting.
fact: Things that are «water-resistant» or «heat-resistant» are not harmed by water or heat.
fact: In science, air resistance is air pushing against a moving object, which slows it down.
fact: «Resist the urge» means stop yourself from doing something you really want to do.
fact: Context tells you which meaning of a word is correct, so read the sentence around it before you decide.
exercise: «The submarine's strong walls resist the squeeze of deep water.» What does resist mean here? | *Stay strong and not be harmed by | Make the water warmer | Let the water in easily | Fight the water like an enemy
exercise: Mia says, «I can't resist the last biscuit.» What does resist mean? | *Stop herself from having it | Share it with her friend | Throw it away | Fight the biscuit
exercise: Air pushes against a falling paper and slows it down. This is called air resistance. What does resist mean in this science idea? | Speed up movement | *Slow down movement | Make a loud sound | Change colour
test: «Pacification means violently crushing the people of a place until they stop resisting.» What does resisting mean here? | Dancing and singing together | *Fighting back against being ruled by force | Going to sleep early | Moving to a new town
test: A watch is described as water-resistant. What does this mean? | *It is not spoiled by water | It only works in the rain | It is full of water | It needs water to work
exam: Which sentence uses resist to mean stop yourself from doing something? | The bridge began to resist the heavy trucks | Our kite would resist the wind and fly higher | *Sam tries hard to resist scratching his mosquito bite | The cat will resist the warm sunshine
